{
  "name": "Train a Causal LM on TinyStories",
  "description": "Pretrain a 203,668,480-parameter GPT-style decoder from scratch, entirely from GUI nodes. TextCorpusDataset streams roneneldan/TinyStories, LMTokenizer (gpt2, 50257 ids) turns it into tokens, and LMTokenizedDataset packs them into 1024-token blocks where the labels are the inputs shifted by one -- that shift IS next-token prediction. Training runs at bf16 with batch 8 and accumulate_steps 4 (an effective batch of 32 sequences, ~32,768 tokens per optimizer step), AdamW at lr 3e-4 with betas 0.9, 0.95 and weight decay 0.1, gradients clipped at 1.0. Afterwards PerplexityEvaluate scores the held-out validation split and TextGenerate continues 'Once upon a time' so you can read what the model learned to say. The corpus is capped at 20,000,000 training and 2,000,000 validation tokens so one epoch finishes in an evening on a 16 GB GPU; clear max_tokens (0 = all) on the LMTokenizedDataset nodes for a real run, and turn on gradient_checkpointing in CausalLMModel if a batch will not fit. The first run downloads TinyStories from the Hugging Face Hub and the gpt2 BPE ranks, so it needs the network once; both are cached afterwards.",
